@startuml 04_-_msrouter_provider_chain
title 04 - msrouter provider chain: GCP (Google Gemini) slot and failover order
skinparam shadowing false
hide empty members
component "Clients - agent loop, CvScorer (finder), apply-worker" as n0
component "msrouter :3000 - ClusterIP, OpenAI-compatible /v1/chat/completions, PAUSED (replicas 0)" as n1
component "EXTRA_PROVIDER_ORDER 1 - unorouter" as n2
component "EXTRA_PROVIDER_ORDER 2 - groq" as n3
component "EXTRA_PROVIDER_ORDER 3 - sambanova" as n4
component "EXTRA_PROVIDER_ORDER 4 - mistral" as n5
component "EXTRA_PROVIDER_ORDER 5 - gemini = GCP (Google Gemini API, GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash-lite)" as n6
component "EXTRA_PROVIDER_ORDER 6 - cline" as n7
component "EXTRA_PROVIDER_ORDER 7 (last) - cloudflare" as n8
component "local slot (on-host LLM providers) - tried before the extras (msrouter config, not facts.md)" as n9
component "pause switch - msrouter.yaml replicas 0 + finder FINDER_SCORING_ENABLED=false" as n10
n0 --> n1 : POST /v1/chat/completions
n1 --> n9 : local slot
n1 --> n2
n1 --> n3
n1 --> n4
n1 --> n5
n1 --> n6
n1 --> n7
n1 --> n8
n10 --> n1 : replicas 0
n10 --> n0 : fallback score 70
note as guide
  GCP is the Google Gemini slot in msrouter
  Base URL: generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai
  Default model: gemini-2.5-flash-lite, free tier via GEMINI_API_KEY.
  Order: unorouter, groq, sambanova, mistral, gemini, cline, cloudflare.
  Cloudflare is last in the walk; the local on-host slot comes first.
  The extras order is the facts.md EXTRA_PROVIDER_ORDER; the primary
  and local slots come from msrouter config, not facts.md.
  Pause switch (moves together): msrouter replicas 0 and finder
  FINDER_SCORING_ENABLED=false -> CvScorer fallback score 70; the
  score >= 60 CV filter stops rejecting and APPLY_MODE stays shadow.
end note

@enduml
